// One authored file holding a whole universe. Heading level sets the structure:
//   #    the universe itself (its identity)
//   ##   a chapter: Sides / Jobs / Narrative / Regions / ...
//   ###  an entry within a chapter (one side, one job type, one story beat)
//
// Each heading's data lives between `---` fences as `Label: value` fact lines, and the
// prose under the fence is what players read.
//
// Almost everything is optional. Reputation axes, standing tuning and the generation
// dials all fall back to engine defaults when you leave them out - which is why this file
// is short. Add chapters as you want them.

# [My Universe](my_universe)
---
Universe
Display: My Universe
---
A small frontier to build on. Two sides, a handful of jobs, and space to fill in.


// ---- The factions. Each heading key IS the side key. `Home` is a system coordinate on
// the galaxy grid; `Offers` names the job types this side hands out.
## [Sides](sides)

### [Iron Concord](iron)
---
Color: #3399ff
Character: military
Disposition: neutral
Home: 6, 4
Values: by-the-book 40, honest 20
Offers: patrol, escort
Flies: 60% Kralien, 40% Arvonian
---
Disciplined and territorial. Respects strength and straight dealing.

### [Ashfall Run](ashfall)
---
Color: #cc6633
Character: outlaw
Disposition: hostile
Home: 2, 7
Offers: salvage
Flies: Torgoth
---
Salvagers who stopped waiting for wrecks to happen on their own.


// ---- Job types the sides above can offer. The engine generates the individual jobs;
// these records say what KINDS exist and what they pay.
## [Jobs](jobs)

### [Patrol](patrol)
---
Reward: 200 credits
---
Sweep a system and clear whatever is hunting in it.

### [Escort](escort)
---
Reward: 250 credits
---
See a freighter safely to its destination.

### [Salvage](salvage)
---
Reward: 150 credits
---
Recover what is worth recovering, and do not ask where it came from.
